# Token Optimization Rules for AI Coding Assistants
# This file helps reduce token usage when using Cursor, Claude Code, Codex, Windsurf

## Core Principles
- Be concise and direct in your requests
- Avoid asking for explanations unless necessary
- Focus on specific changes rather than broad refactoring
- Use file paths instead of describing file contents
- Request code-only outputs when possible

## When Asking for Changes
- Specify exact file paths and line numbers
- Ask for minimal changes to achieve the goal
- Avoid "explain why" - just ask for the fix
- Use "change X to Y" instead of "rewrite this function"

## Code Review Requests
- Ask for specific issue types: "check for security issues" not "review this code"
- Limit scope: "review lines 50-100" instead of "review this file"
- Request fixes only: "fix any bugs" not "explain and fix bugs"

## Documentation
- Only request docstrings for public APIs
- Ask for inline comments only for complex logic
- Skip documentation for obvious code

## Testing
- Ask for specific test cases rather than comprehensive test suites
- Focus on edge cases you're concerned about
- Request test code only, not explanations

## Refactoring
- Request specific refactoring: "extract this function" not "improve code quality"
- Limit scope to single files when possible
- Avoid "make it more efficient" - be specific about what to optimize

## Context Management
- Provide only relevant file contents
- Use @file references instead of pasting code
- Remove unnecessary context from conversations
- Clear conversation history when starting new tasks
